= December 2023 — The promised coalition has another claimant

KO is not in Prime Minister **[+ prime_minister +]**'s cabinet. Lewica chose
[? if formation_coalition_code = "left_p2050": Poland 2050?][? if
formation_coalition_code = "left_psl": PSL?][? if formation_coalition_code =
"left_third": the whole Third Way?] and proved that the majority can govern
without the largest democratic opposition party.

[? if sejm_list_outcome = "democratic_8": That arithmetic is legal and the
political wound is exceptional. KO says voters were asked to support one
**Broad Democratic Coalition** and then watched Lewica use its seats to deny
KO every ministry. Tusk's caucus treats the common-list promise as broken and
turns opposition to the cabinet into its organising principle.?][? if
sejm_list_outcome != "democratic_8": KO still calls the exclusion a theft of
the democratic mandate, but it cannot point to a single filed committee as a
contract. Its answer is the same: a harder, more right-leaning opposition
designed to squeeze both the government and PiS.?]

KO will cooperate on constitutional repair only when it can claim authorship.
On budgets, appointments and the next election it now campaigns against the
cabinet as fiercely as it campaigns against PiS.

- @ko_exclusion_keep_channel
- @ko_exclusion_own_choice

