= December 2023 — The excluded partner chooses a side

The coalition agreement admits [? if formation_coalition_code =
"ko_p2050_left": KO, ?]Poland 2050 and Lewica while leaving PSL outside. [? if
formation_coalition_code = "left_p2050": KO is excluded too, but PSL's
delegates blame their own Third Way partner for taking ministries while the
agrarian party that helped win the mandate receives none.?][? if
formation_coalition_code = "ko_p2050_left": For PSL delegates, the loss is
larger than a missing ministry: Poland 2050 has used the Third Way mandate to
enter government without the agrarian party which helped win it.?]

Władysław Kosiniak-Kamysz cannot persuade the national council that continued
centrist bargaining will restore PSL's leverage. He is removed. [? if
psl_2023_exclusion_successor = "Piotr Zgorzelski": The conservative
parliamentary wing is stronger than the county pragmatists, so **Piotr
Zgorzelski** wins the succession on a promise to negotiate only with the
right.?][? if psl_2023_exclusion_successor = "Marek Sawicki": The county
machine outweighs the parliamentary conservatives and rallies around **Marek
Sawicki**, who reaches the same strategic conclusion in a more agrarian
language: future government talks will be held only with the right.?]

This is PSL's congress decision, not Lewica's appointment. We can keep an
opposition channel open or defend the coalition choice and compete directly
for rural voters. Neither response restores the democratic option PSL has
closed.

