= December 2023 — The excluded partner starts again

The coalition agreement admits KO, PSL and Lewica while leaving Poland 2050
outside. The Third Way bargain is over, but **Szymon Hołownia** refuses the
conclusion that his movement must now choose one of the two largest parties.

He keeps the chair and announces a second founding congress: anti-PiS because
the state cannot return to party capture, anti-KO because replacing one
patronage system with another is not renewal. Volunteers who were drifting
toward Konfederacja hear an anti-establishment offer without its nationalist
programme. Poland 2050 gains polling momentum at Konfederacja's expense.

The relaunch also gives Hołownia a real chance of surviving the leadership
reckoning after the 2025 presidential cycle. It is not immunity: a presidential
victory would still make party leadership constitutionally incompatible, and
a weak movement can still reject its founder. For now, his independence has
raised the ceiling.

This is Poland 2050's decision. Lewica can recognise an independent competitor
or defend the cabinet bargain and challenge it for the same voters.

- @p2050_comeback_channel
- @p2050_comeback_compete

